#. Diagram label
msgid "A fact is needed that no file holds"
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:66
#. Diagram label
msgid "Answer, or decline"
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Before asking. A repository whose root already holds a declaration, `<name>.json`, is not a blank slate, and a question whose candidates the agent could have worked out itself wastes the one question it is entitled to."
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:112
#. Diagram label
msgid "declined"
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:11
#. Diagram label
msgid "Determine the harness and repositories"
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:72
#. Diagram label
msgid "Does the answer settle it?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:37
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Filled interchangeably by a person or a sibling agent that already holds the answer — the output records which, since the two are evidence of different weight, but this lane's standing to answer is the same either way. Declining is a legitimate exit here, not a failure: it is what turns the outcome into \"unsettled\" rather than forcing a guess."
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:98
#. Diagram label
msgid "Harness and repositories determined"
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:25
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Holds the one judgement this process refuses to compute: whether an answer actually settles the question, which is why G_Settled carries no folio:decision unlike the DMN-backed gateways elsewhere in this corpus. It narrows candidates before spending the one question a reader is entitled to, and closes either with a determination or, on a decline, with what is still open — never a guess standing in for either."
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:24
#. Diagram label
msgid "Initiator"
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:73
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Judgement, exercised by the Initiator — which is why this gateway carries no `folio:decision`. Whether an answer settles the matter is not computable from the answer's text, and a DMN table here would be a claim that it is."
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:47
#. Diagram label
msgid "Narrow the candidates from context"
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:111
#. Diagram label
msgid "not yet — ask once more"
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:56
#. Diagram label
msgid "Put the question, with its candidates named"
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:80
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record the determination"
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:89
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record what is still open"
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:36
#. Diagram label
msgid "Requestor"
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:102
#. Diagram label
msgid "Still open, and said so"
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:90
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The declined route. `outcome: unsettled` with `stillOpen`, so the next actor resumes rather than restarts. An agent that reaches for a default here has produced a guess, not a determination."
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:67
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The Requestor lane, filled by a person or by a sibling agent. Declining is a permitted move and not an error: it produces `outcome: unsettled` with what is still open, never a guess."
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:14
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "THE SECOND PROCESS IN CAT_BOOTSTRAP, and an exception to bootstrap holding as little as possible. Two facts have no answer in any file an Initiator can reach: WHICH harness this repository should become, and WHICH repositories are read from and written to. No instruction body produces them — they are judgements held by whoever asked for the harness. An agent that cannot obtain them cannot take the first step of `initialize-harness`, so this is presupposed by every task rather than indicated by one. (Logging sits differently and is NOT the contrast it first looks like: the owner's rule is \"logging is optional, unless indicated on tasks\", and `initialize-harness` indicates it — which is why `log-message` is here too.) SYMMETRIC IN ITS PARTICIPANTS. Human-to-agent and agent-to-agent are the same process: the Requestor lane is filled by a person or by a sibling agent that already holds the answer. The output records which, because the two are evidence of different weight, but neither is refused and they are not conflated. THE TOOL DOES NOT DECIDE. `discuss` carries a question out and an answer back. Judgement — the Initiator's — chooses what to ask and rules on when an answer settles the matter. The task is finished when a document conforming to `discussion.output.schema.json` exists, not when a pleasant exchange has occurred. PRECONDITION: the Initiator has read bootstrap/README.md and has narrowed the candidates as far as context allows. BPMN has no precondition element and this schema adds none yet, so it is stated here as `initialize-harness` states its own, and tracked as bean `lv3j`. NO folio:bean on any activity, and isExecutable is false, for the reasons `initialize-harness` gives: a bean is work-plan machinery and an engine is harness machinery, and an Initiator runs before either exists. This is data an Initiator reads."
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:57
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Uses the `discuss` tool. One question where one will do — the Initiator's persona is \"asks exactly one question when it must\". A question a reader must go and research is not ready to be asked."
msgstr ""

#: processes/discussion.bpmn:81
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Writes a document conforming to `discussion.output.schema.json`: the harness, the repositories as read-from / written-to pairs, `determinedBy`, and who answered. This artefact is what finishes the task."
msgstr ""

